From e15bea1a6a4ad934bc0227b45fc58a8b7ed1f92b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VPinInfinite <340424849+VPinInfinite@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] ssf: DOF's SSFImpactController, its sounds played through
 miniaudio

Ported from DirectOutput's SSFImpactController.cs (Kai "MrKai" Cherry's, MIT)
for Visual Pinball Infinite, under DOF's names and settings, so a Cabinet.xml
written for DOF works unchanged: 15 outputs (flippers, slingshots, six
bumpers, knocker, shaker, gear, hellball motor, bell), each hit restarting
DOF's impact sound on the front and rear exciter pairs at the flipper, bumper
or slingshot level, the shaker and gear motors looping DOF's own sounds on
the bass shakers, the levels and speakers from FrontExciters, RearExciters,
BassShaker1 and 2, LowImpactMode, DeviceNumber, ImpactFactor,
ShakerImpactFactor, FlipperLevel, BumperLevel, SlingsLevel and GearLevel.

DOF plays them through BASS, which is closed and can't ship; SSFBass.cpp
stands in for the BASS calls it makes, mixing with miniaudio (David Reid's,
public domain or MIT No Attribution; its header from VPX 5436's bundle,
0.11.25, compiled privately into libdof): each speaker flag lays a sound on
the pair BASS lays out (front, rear, centre and LFE, side, then numbered
pairs, by the device's speaker count), a flag a device lacks refused with
BASS's speaker error, as DOF's logs report it; devices numbered as BASS
numbers them (1 the default, then each output). DOF's three sounds (SSF1C,
7hzOD, OG) are embedded from sounds/, its licence beside them.

VPI_SSF_CAPTURE=<file.wav> plays nothing and writes the mix, eight channels
at 48 kHz, to that file: the way to check it with no speakers sounding.

Differences: the logs name the sound device, not BASS; the shaker's loops
are made once (DOF made a new one on every speed change when BassShaker1 is
None, leaving the old ones playing); BASS resamples with its own filter.
